# Disabling the walter-modem protocols this pager never uses
# (CONFIG_WALTER_MODEM_ENABLE_SOCKETS/_HTTP/_COAP/_BLUECHERRY) to
# reclaim RTC memory and flash. All four symbols exist, but every one of
# them (individually and together) FAILS TO BUILD against v1.5.0 as checked
# out here: WalterModem.cpp's _dispatchEvent() unconditionally references
# handler->httpHandler/coapHandler/socketHandler and WalterModemEvent's
# ev->http/coap/socket members without a matching #if guard, and the MOTA
# firmware-upgrade code unconditionally references _blueCherry.ota_buffer
# even though _blueCherry itself is declared inside
# `#if CONFIG_WALTER_MODEM_ENABLE_BLUECHERRY`. Disabling any of these four
# options breaks the vendor library's own compilation, not just ours.
#
# The managed component is never patched in place (firmware/README.md), so
# none of these are disabled here. The RTC memory pressure this was meant to
# relieve is instead addressed by sizing modes.c's own RTC struct to fit the
# ~7kB the library already consumes in this configuration (see
# modes_boot()'s sizeof() log).

# F3.1 (docs/DEVICE_TASKS.md): custom partition table — nvs/assets/otadata
# plus two OTA app slots, docs/DEVICE_PLAN.md §3.4. Flash size follows the
# real Walter module (16 MB, DEVICE_PLAN.md §5.1), not the ESP-IDF generic
# 2 MB default, which is too small for this layout.
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM=y
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME="partitions.csv"
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_16MB=y
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE="16MB"

# F3.5 (docs/DEVICE_TASKS.md): setup.c's setup_derive() needs mbedtls_hkdf()
# for the setup code's bid/bpw/bkey derivation (docs/DEVICE_PLAN.md §3.2);
# off by default in ESP-IDF 5.2's mbedtls Kconfig.
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_HKDF_C=y

# This board exposes exactly one USB connector, wired to the ESP32-S3's
# native USB-Serial/JTAG peripheral -- UART0's own RX/TX pins (the
# ESP-IDF default console) go nowhere reachable from that connector. Found
# on real hardware: main.c's Setup-mode console (`setup <code>`) was bound
# to UART0 and silently could not be typed into over the flashing/monitor
# cable, even though boot/log output appeared fine (log output already
# went out over USB-Serial/JTAG as the *secondary* console). Promoting it
# to the *primary* console unifies input and output on the one connection
# that actually exists, and is required for esp_console_new_repl_usb_
# serial_jtag() (main.c) to even compile -- that API is gated behind this
# exact Kconfig symbol, not the secondary-console one.
CONFIG_ESP_CONSOLE_USB_SERIAL_JTAG=y

# modes_run() runs on the main task and drives ui/gfx, mbedtls HMAC and the
# modem library; the 3584-byte default overflowed on hardware. Same size the
# setup REPL task already needed (main.c).
CONFIG_ESP_MAIN_TASK_STACK_SIZE=16384

# v0.2: TLS profile 3 is used for the CA fetch (docs/V02_DESIGN.md 4.4). The vendored modem
# library's Kconfig default is now 6, but an existing sdkconfig keeps whatever it had (3), and
# then tlsConfigProfile(3) fails locally with NO_SUCH_PROFILE. Found on hardware 2026-09-20.
# Pin it here so every build tree gets it.
CONFIG_WALTER_MODEM_MAX_TLS_PROFILES=6

# Watchdogs (main/watchdog.c). The task watchdog must reboot, not just print:
# an unattended pager that stalls has to come back by itself. 60 s (the Kconfig
# maximum) because the
# main loop has legitimate waits of tens of seconds (modem recovery, assistance
# data download); the loop feeds it every pass.
CONFIG_ESP_TASK_WDT_PANIC=y
CONFIG_ESP_TASK_WDT_TIMEOUT_S=60

# docs/WIFI_TASKS.md W5: esp-mqtt over the ESP32-S3's own WiFi station.
# WPA2-PSK STA only -- docs/WIFI_DESIGN.md §4 explicitly rejects a SoftAP
# setup portal ("DEVICE_PLAN.md §3.0 already rejected ... at ~450 kB of
# Wi-Fi stack"), and this device never runs a websocket transport (esp-mqtt
# always dials the broker directly over TLS, same broker LTE already uses).
# Both trimmed for flash headroom (design §8's flash risk; W0's own
# before/after measurement never ran on this branch -- see the task report).
# WPA3-Personal (CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_ENABLE_WPA3_SAE) and MQTT-over-SSL
# (CONFIG_MQTT_TRANSPORT_SSL) are left at their ESP-IDF defaults (both `y`)
# -- WPA3 costs nothing extra to leave enabled (a WPA2/WPA3 transition AP
# still associates as WPA2) and MQTT-over-SSL is required.
CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_SOFTAP_SUPPORT=n
CONFIG_WS_TRANSPORT=n

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# W6 (2026-09-23, build/bench-logs/phaseAG-wifi.log): the first WiFi bench
# session associated and got a DHCP lease, then died at
# `mbedtls_ssl_setup returned -0x7F00` = MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_ALLOC_FAILED. Root
# cause is RAM, not TLS: this board has 132,684 B of DRAM heap in three
# regions (75+21+32 KiB, no PSRAM) and 80,212 B free at boot
# (phaseAF-boot.log:54), esp_wifi+lwIP take ~45-52 kB of that (estimate --
# wifi_sta.c now logs the real number), and mbedtls_ssl_setup() then wants
# ONE CONTIGUOUS MBEDTLS_SSL_IN_CONTENT_LEN + ~300 B block, which at 16384
# was 16,685 B. Every value below is WiFi-path-only: `grep -n esp_tls\|
# mbedtls_ssl firmware/main/*.c*` finds no user outside xport_wifi.c's error
# reporting -- the LTE path does TLS inside the Sequans modem, and
# setup.c/auth.c use mbedtls only for HKDF/HMAC/SHA, which none of these
# symbols touch. So none of this can regress LTE.
#
# NOTE for whoever flashes next: an existing firmware/sdkconfig OVERRIDES
# this file (same trap CONFIG_WALTER_MODEM_MAX_TLS_PROFILES documents
# above, and the reason the two W5 lines above never reached the phaseAG
# image -- CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_SOFTAP_SUPPORT was still y in it). Delete
# firmware/sdkconfig and `idf.py reconfigure` before the next bench build,
# then check these values in the regenerated file.

# 16384 -> 8192: halves the single contiguous block the handshake needs
# (16,685 -> 8,493 B). The incoming flight must still fit one record:
# EMQX serverless sends leaf + one DigiCert intermediate, ~2.8 kB DER, so
# ServerHello+Certificate+ServerKeyExchange+Done is ~3.3 kB -- 2.5x margin.
# 4096 would probably also work and is NOT taken: it has no margin for a
# broker certificate rotation that adds a chain link.
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_IN_CONTENT_LEN=8192
# 4096 -> 2048. Largest thing this device ever sends is a 640 B envelope
# plus MQTT/TLS framing (PROTOCOL.md §3.3). CONFIG_MBEDTLS_ASYMMETRIC_
# CONTENT_LEN is already y, which is what lets these two differ.
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_OUT_CONTENT_LEN=2048
# Allocate the record buffers per-record instead of at mbedtls_ssl_setup()
# time, and free them when idle: this is the option that turns the two
# numbers above from a peak into a transient. Blocked only by DTLS and TLS
# 1.3 (mbedtls Kconfig:100-110, :176-178); both are already off here.
# CONFIG_MBEDTLS_DYNAMIC_FREE_CONFIG_DATA is deliberately NOT set: its own
# help text says the caller must re-register the certificate and private key
# afterwards, and it saves ~2 kB against a real correctness risk on the
# reconnect path.
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_DYNAMIC_BUFFER=y
# docs/WIFI_DESIGN.md §5 rejects ESP-IDF's certificate bundle as a second,
# weaker trust store ("one rule is better"); nothing calls
# esp_crt_bundle_attach(). It is still being linked: build/esp-idf/mbedtls/
# x509_crt_bundle is 64,057 B of the 661 kB app image. Flash only, no RAM
# effect -- taken here because it is free.
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE=n

# esp_wifi buffers. ESP-IDF's own ESP32-S3 rank table
# (docs/en/api-guides/wifi.rst, "How to Configure Parameters") puts
# static_rx/dynamic_rx/dynamic_tx at 8/32/32 for "Default" and 3/6/6 for
# "Minimum", 183.9 vs 273.6 kB available. This pager's traffic is one <=640 B
# MQTT message every few minutes, so throughput is irrelevant; take a point
# between the two ranks.
# 10 -> 6: -4 x 1600 B = 6,400 B freed permanently at esp_wifi_init().
CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_STATIC_RX_BUFFER_NUM=6
# 32 -> 12: a cap, not an allocation -- lowers the worst-case burst peak by
# ~20 x 1600 = 32 kB, which is what protects a handshake from a burst
# arriving mid-flight. Keeps CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_RX_BA_WIN=6 legal
# (wifi.rst: BA win <= min(2 x static_rx, dynamic_rx) = min(12, 12)).
CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_DYNAMIC_RX_BUFFER_NUM=12
# 32 -> 12: same shape, ~30 kB off the TX peak.
CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_DYNAMIC_TX_BUFFER_NUM=12
